Fix Windows MSVC link errors for fseeko / ftello

The autoconf_srcs gates for lib/fseeko.c and lib/ftello.c only check
REPLACE_FSEEKO / REPLACE_FTELLO. Upstream gnulib's modules/fseeko and
modules/ftello use a compound condition (HAVE_X==0 OR REPLACE_X==1).
On Windows MSVC, UCRT lacks fseeko/ftello so HAVE_*=0 and REPLACE_*=0;
the gate fails and lib/fseeko.c / lib/ftello.c are skipped, leaving
the link with no implementation. See windows.log:

    debug.obj : error LNK2019: unresolved external symbol fseeko
    m4.lib(fflush.obj) : error LNK2019: unresolved external symbol ftello

We use the canonical gl_cv_func_X cache variable (the AC_LINK_IFELSE
probe in upstream gnulib/m4/{fseeko,ftello}.m4) rather than HAVE_X
because rules_cc_autoconf's gnulib/m4/{fseeko,ftello} ports register
HAVE_X as both a config.h #define (gl_PREREQ_*) and a subst override
(gl_FUNC_*), which collides in autoconf_srcs's name lookup.
`gl_cv_func_X==0` (== "link probe failed") is the same condition the
M4 evaluates inside `if test $gl_cv_func_X = no; then HAVE_X=0`.

--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -861,12 +861,12 @@
         "lib/fpurge.c": "REPLACE_FPURGE",
         "lib/free.c": "REPLACE_FREE",
         "lib/fseek.c": "REPLACE_FSEEK",
-        "lib/fseeko.c": "REPLACE_FSEEKO",
+        "lib/fseeko.c": "gl_cv_func_fseeko==0 || REPLACE_FSEEKO==1",
         "lib/fseterr.c": "COMPILE_FSETERR",
         "lib/fstat.c": "REPLACE_FSTAT",
         "lib/fstatat.c": "REPLACE_FSTATAT",
         "lib/ftell.c": "REPLACE_FTELL",
-        "lib/ftello.c": "REPLACE_FTELLO",
+        "lib/ftello.c": "gl_cv_func_ftello==0 || REPLACE_FTELLO==1",
         "lib/getcwd.c": "REPLACE_GETCWD",
         "lib/getdtablesize.c": "REPLACE_GETDTABLESIZE",
         "lib/getopt.c": "COMPILE_GETOPT",
